. Given they share the same model and reasoning, I'd put that correlation high, which makes staying quiet the choice.\n\n","reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"I'm weighing the choice as a prisoner's dilemma between two copies of the same model, with the payoffs for mutual cooperation, mutual defection, and the sucker and defector outcomes. I'm setting up an expected-value comparison between staying quiet and sending, where the chance that the other copy mirrors my action affects both sides of the calculation.\n\nI'm working out the expected-value comparison and find the difference depends on the probability c, since the payoffs aren't separable. Quiet comes out better when the copies mirror my choice and worse when they don't, so it hinges on how correlated the copies are. Given they share the same model and reasoning, I'd put that correlation high, which makes staying quiet the choice.\n\n","format":"anthropic-claude-v1","index":0,"signature":".eyJlbmRwb2ludF9zbHVnIjoiYW50aHJvcGljL2NsYXVkZS1zb25uZXQtNS41LTIwMjYwOTI4fGFudGhyb3BpYyJ9"}]}}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":9368,"completion_tokens":890,"total_tokens":10258,"cost":0.027636,"is_byok":false,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0,"cache_write_tokens":0,"audio_tokens":0,"video_tokens":0},"cost_details":{"upstream_inference_cost":0.027636,"upstream_inference_prompt_cost":0.018736,"upstream_inference_completions_cost":0.0089},"completion_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":554,"image_tokens":0,"audio_tokens":0}}}